Patch 7930 (diagnostic, rollback netcode stalls): the [RSXMEM] line also shows video memory usage and budget.

Why. test11 research (RESEARCH-TEST12.md) placed the desktop's 66-83 ms "present" runs inside render_frame_prepare's full GPU wait, so
the GPU itself was slow for whole runs of frames. One suspect is video memory over-commit: when a process's GPU memory use goes over
the budget the OS gives it, the video memory manager pages resources in and out and GPU work stalls. Nothing in the logs showed it.

What. At init the device's adapter is kept as IDXGIAdapter3 (EnumAdapterByLuid on the device's LUID; NULL where the interface is
missing). The [RSXMEM] line (patch 2016, every 30 s, on the thread that presents) now ends with
  vram_local=<usage>/<budget>MB vram_nonlocal=<usage>/<budget>MB
from QueryVideoMemoryInfo (local = the card's own memory, non-local = shared system memory), or " vram=?" without the adapter. Two
queries per line, never on a per-frame path. The new fields are appended, so readers of the older fields keep working. Usage over
budget means the OS is paging this process's GPU memory. The adapter is released at shutdown.

